---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'About teleprompter.wtf Studio | Free Video Recording';
const description =
  'teleprompter.wtf is an open-source, local-first teleprompter and video recorder. Record beside the lens or use the classic presenter without an account.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose-page section-wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span>
    </nav>
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p><h1>Make the video. Keep the file.</h1><p>
        teleprompter.wtf is a free, open-source tool for creators and speakers. Write a script, read
        it beside the lens and record in your browser.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h2>Why Studio exists</h2><p>
        Recording a talking-head video should not require an account or subscription. Studio puts
        the script near the camera, keeps takes locally and lets you save the file to your device.
      </p>
      <h2>The classic presenter remains</h2><p>
        If you only need scrolling text, use the <a href="/#classic-editor">classic teleprompter</a
        >. It supports manual pace, mirror mode and keyboard control without opening a camera.
      </p>
      <h2>Open source and local</h2><p>
        There is no script or recording server. The site uses self-hosted Umami for page views and
        product events, without script text or file names. Inspect the <a
          href="https://github.com/SABYA648/Telemprompter-WTF">source code</a
        > or read the <a href="/privacy">storage details</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a browser-specific issue, open a GitHub issue with steps to reproduce and your browser
        version. Please leave private scripts and recordings out of reports.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
